# try_get_individual / try_get_literal / axiom_parser.rs multiple-owl:members
# panic sites, which are a separate follow-up under the same issue.

ghpull:418 a bl:PullRequest, bl:WorkItem ;
    rdfs:label "rdf_owl_translator: return Err instead of panicking on malformed rdf:List (#363)" ;
    bl:number 418 ;
    bl:state bl:Open .

session:claudeSonnet5 a prov:SoftwareAgent ;
    rdfs:label "Claude Sonnet 5" .

session:pr418 a agp:AgentSession ;
    prov:wasAssociatedWith session:claudeSonnet5 ;
    prov:used ghissues:363 ;
    prov:startedAtTime "2026-08-07T15:00:00Z"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    prov:endedAtTime "2026-08-07T15:52:41Z"^^xsd:dateTime .

session:pr418Summary a agp:TranscriptSummary ;
    agp:summaryText "Sixth cluster from issue #363's panic-on-malformed-input catalogue, and the biggest one so far: rdf_owl_translator::ingress::get_rdf_list_elements panicked on three shapes of structurally malformed rdf:List encoding -- a cyclic rdf:rest chain, a node with != 1 rdf:first triples, a node with != 1 rdf:rest triples. rdf:List backs owl:intersectionOf, owl:unionOf, owl:members (AllDisjointClasses/Properties), owl:disjointUnionOf, owl:propertyChainAxiom and owl:onProperties, so the panic was reachable from almost anywhere in a Turtle-encoded OWL ontology, crashing --serve on load. Followed the plan doc's scope decision (already on main): fix get_rdf_list_elements alone, leave try_get_individual/try_get_literal/axiom_parser.rs's two multiple-owl:members panics as a follow-up -- threading Result through those would have roughly doubled the diff for a different class of malformed input. Added TranslatorError::MalformedRdfList(String) (no existing error type in the crate, confirmed by grep). Threaded the Result along two independent paths: class_expression_parser.rs's collect_anon_class_exprs (owl:oneOf and intersectionOf/unionOf branches) and build_restriction's owl:onProperties branch, both reached via OntologyDeclarations::build; and axiom_parser.rs's extract_axiom, which calls get_rdf_list_elements in four match arms nested inside a large match-on-predicate that used to return Option<Axiom> directly. Rather than converting every Some/None in that ~250-line match, the whole match was left as the tail of an outer Ok(match {...}) -- ? and return have type ! and coerce regardless of the arm's expected type, so only seven Option-returning res.get_named_resource(...)? spots needed converting to let-else early returns; the four get_rdf_list_elements calls just got a trailing ?. build_restriction was split into itself (the one fallible owl:onProperties branch) plus build_restriction_rest (the unchanged infallible remainder), avoiding a rewrite of ~15 unrelated require_triple_obj(...)? Option-uses. This mirrors PR #407 (eli2rl.rs)'s style, confirmed by reading that diff first -- same shape of threading fallibility through a small recursive translation layer, Result instead of Option, but no silent-skip: a malformed list fails the whole rdf2owl call, per the plan's intent that this is a load-time hard error. rdf2owl (translator.rs) changed to Result<OntologyDocument, TranslatorError>; all callers across the workspace were updated (src/lib.rs's compile_ontology_rules/run_owlrl_reasoning via map_err+?, dagalog-kernel's dispatch_cell likewise, benches, and ~20 test call sites via .unwrap() on known-good fixtures). TDD: four unit tests in ingress.rs build malformed/well-formed lists directly via Datastore::add_triple + create_unnamed_anon_resource (cyclic/wrong-count lists aren't expressible via Turtle's list sugar), confirmed red against the pre-fix panics by inspection, then green. One integration test in tests/owl_integration.rs loads a hand-written Turtle owl:intersectionOf list missing its rdf:rest, asserting Err(MalformedRdfList) through rdf2owl; had to avoid {:?}-formatting the whole Result since OntologyDocument isn't Debug, and clippy's unreachable-pattern lint caught an unnecessary catch-all arm given the enum has one variant. Branch had drifted one commit behind origin/main (docs-only); rebase was clean. Full quality gate -- fmt --check, clippy -D warnings, test --workspace -- run post-rebase with fresh results: all green, zero regressions." ;
    agp:reasoningFor ghpull:418 ;
    prov:wasGeneratedBy session:pr418 ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo session:claudeSonnet5 .
